# Design System evolution (Play’Up web)

Operational SoT: `src/PlayUp/web/docs/design-system.md`. Product intent: Notion **Identité visuelle**.

## Gate — every visual change

Before shipping UI/CSS in Play’Up web, answer:

1. **Is this a one-off page quirk?** → page-local CSS (`pages/*.css`) only if foundations cannot express it.
2. **Is this a reusable visual language?** → evolve the design system (tokens / foundations / thin React primitives).
3. **If the DS evolves** → update **FoundationsPlayground** (`/dev/foundations`) in the **same** change. No silent DS growth without playground coverage.

> Foundations define the language; the playground verifies it; the Shell consumes it; legacy pages stay temporarily outside.

## What counts as DS evolution

- New or changed semantic tokens (`--color-*`, spacing, radius, …)
- New or changed foundations (`.ds-*` recipes)
- New shared React primitives over foundations (`Status`, `TeamCrest`, …)
- New shared icons meant for multiple surfaces

**Not** DS evolution: copy/i18n, page composition/layout wiring, Read-driven prominence, one-off spacing tweaks that stay page-local.

## Playground duty

- Route `/dev/foundations` is the **terrain of truth** — not Storybook.
- New foundation / token / primitive → visible demo section (usage + anti-usage when useful).
- Do not demo full Shell or full product pages in the playground (except minimal chrome rail / composition sketches already established).

## Anti-patterns

- Inventing a parallel mini-system in page CSS when a foundation should exist
- Expanding foundations “just in case” without a real reuse need (`no-cargo-cult.mdc`)
- Changing tokens/foundations without playground + `docs/design-system.md` when the public API or budget changes
- Migrating all pages in a big-bang — apply `docs/page-migration.md` when a product task already touches the page

## Docs

- Token budget / layers / legacy boundary → update `docs/design-system.md`
- Product/visual truth change → Notion Identité / Expérience produit (per `documentation.mdc`)
